uous water impact or rushing water. A waterfall (A), static noise (B), and a running shower (D) all share acoustic properties (rushing water or white noise) that could lead to confusion with rain. A car engine starting involves distinct mechanical noises (cranking, combustion) that are acoustically dissimilar to rain.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
