2025-12-24 16:57:03 | INFO | Q577 id=fb444a47-feba-4daf-b8ef-e158c9000798 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The audio presents a musical excerpt that appears to be in a minor key, based on the general mood and the presence of a prominent $\text{B}\flat$ chord. The question asks for the harmonic function of the $\text{B}\flat$ chord within the context of the $\text{C}$ minor key.\n\n1.  **Identify the key:** The question explicitly states the key is $\text{C}$ minor.\n2.  **Determine the scale degrees in $\text{C}$ minor:** The notes in the $\text{C}$ natural minor scale are $\text{C}$ (1), $\text{D}$ ($\text{ii}^{\circ}$), $\text{E}\flat$ ($\text{iii}$), $\text{F}$ ($\text{iv}$), $\text{G}$ ($\text{v}$ or $\text{V}$), $\text{A}\flat$ ($\text{VI}$), $\text{B}\flat$ ($\text{VII}$).\n3.  **Identify the chord built on $\text{B}\flat$ in $\text{C}$ minor:** A triad built on the seventh scale degree ($\text{B}\flat$) in the natural minor scale ($\text{C}$ natural minor: $\text{C}, \text{D}, \text{E}\flat, \text{F}, \text{G}, \text{A}\flat, \text{B}\flat$) is a major chord ($\text{B}\flat - \text{D} - \text{F}$). This chord is the $\text{VII}$ chord.\n4.  **Determine the function of the $\text{VII}$ chord in minor keys:**\n    *   The tonic is $\text{i}$ ($\text{Cm}$).\n    *   The subdominant is $\text{iv}$ ($\text{Fm}$) or $\text{iv}^6$ ($\text{A}\flat$ major).\n    *   The dominant is $\text{V}$ ($\text{G}$ major) or $\text{v}$ ($\text{Gm}$).\n    *   The chord built on the lowered leading tone (the $\text{VII}$ chord, $\text{B}\flat$ major in $\text{C}$ minor) is traditionally called the **subtonic** chord. It functions as a pre-dominant or sometimes as a substitute for the tonic, but its specific label derived from the scale degree is the subtonic.\n\n5.  **Evaluate the options based on the $\text{VII}$ chord:**\n    *   A) tonic ($\text{i}$ or $\text{Cm}$) - Incorrect.\n    *   B) subdominant ($\text{iv