d the second speaker is neutral.)\nC) both speakers remain neutral throughout. (Incorrect. The first speaker shows a reaction to the requirement.)\nD) first speaker shows surprise; second remains neutral. (This is identical to A.)\n\nSince A and D are identical and accurately reflect the analysis (First speaker shows a reaction/surprise to the requirement, Second speaker remains neutral), I will select A based on the initial presentation.\n\nReasoning: The first speaker expresses mild surprise or concern when asked for her original birth certificate ("My my original birth certificate? But I don't carry that with me."). The second speaker maintains a professional and neutral tone throughout the exchange while processing the application and stating the requirements.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{A}$
